{
  "name": "glide_strafe",
  "note": "(anim-rework S3 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) The glide strafe, weapon drawn, written for a step to the RIGHT (the left strafe is this clip mirrored by the wiring): a shuffle step that never crosses the feet: the lead (right) foot lifts low and steps out (about 23 cm between the ankles at its widest, a 15 cm step), the weight moves onto it, then the trailing (left) foot closes in to a narrow stance (about 10 cm between the ankles, the knees inside the hips) without passing the right; knees soft and over the feet (18-38 deg), the pelvis level and facing forward (no yaw), the trunk square at the ready stance. Not mirrored (8 keys, one step cycle). Legs, pelvis and trunk only: the arms are keyed neutral (hanging, elbows 10) because the weapon arms stay procedural (hand IK on the gun). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
